# =====================================================================
#  .gitignore  —  keeps the trial data OUT of GitHub
#  Rule of thumb: code goes up, anything made FROM the data stays home.
#  NOTE: .gitignore only stops NEW files. If a file was already
#  committed, ignoring it now does NOT remove it from history.
# =====================================================================

# ---- 1. The data folder: only its README and placeholder go up ----
data/*
!data/README.md
!data/.gitkeep

# ---- 2. Data file types, wherever they are in the repo ----
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.parquet
*.feather
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.joblib
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.json
*.sqlite
*.db

# ---- 3. Geospatial / imagery (plots, orthomosaics, QGIS projects) ----
*.tif
*.tiff
*.gpkg
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.cpg
*.qgz
*.qgs

# ---- 4. Outputs and figures (figures are drawn from real plot data) ----
figures/*
!figures/.gitkeep
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.svg
*.pdf

# ---- 5. Notebooks and HTML exports (their saved outputs contain data) ----
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.html

# ---- 6. Private files that must never go up ----
private_terms.txt
leak_audit*

# ---- 7. Python / editor / OS clutter ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# ---- 8. Local handover notes (contain absolute paths to the data folder) ----
HANDOVER.md
HANDOVER_report.txt

# ---- 9. preprocessing/ artefacts, redacted copies, deliberately tracked ----
# Sections 3 and 5 above ignore *.qgz and *.ipynb everywhere. These two are
# wanted in the repo, so they are re-included here. The committed copies are
# REDACTED (cluster paths and usernames replaced with __REDACTED_*__ markers);
# the unredacted originals live outside the repo. See preprocessing/README.md.
!preprocessing/16_texture_extraction_bluebear.ipynb
# potato_pipeline.qgz stays ignored. Redacting its paths did not make it safe:
# the project file records the trial's map extent, which pins the field site to
# within a few metres. That is a disclosure decision about the trial, not about
# the author, so it needs the data owner's call. Add
# "!preprocessing/potato_pipeline.qgz" here once that is settled.
